To achieve this, you'll need to use the `llama` command-line tool with the 
`-c` option to provide a string of Python code as input. Then, you can 
pipe the output to another `llama` instance using the `-v` option to 
enable verbose mode and allow us to take control of the session.

Here's an example workflow:

